1	//! FM-1 SoC: memory map + peripherals.
2	//!
3	//! Memory map (recon + Felucca HAL headers + corpus literals):
4	//!   0x0200_0000  XIP flash (app window) — code runs from here
5	//!   0x01c0_0000  data RAM (≥512 KiB; BOOT_STATE at 0x01C7FD80 observed)
6	//!   0x5000_0-    GPIO ports A..H (0x40 stride: OUT+0, DIR+8, DIE+C, PU+10, PD+14)
7	//!   0x5100_|     IOMAP
8	//!   0x1000_-0x1002  clock
9	//!   0x1080_0/0x1090_0  TIMER4/TIMER5 (CNT reads = synthetic progress)
10	//!   0x11c0_0-    SPI0 = external NOR flash (model in spiflash.rs; CS = PD0)
11	//!   0x11d0_0-    SPI1 = LCD (ST7789-class 240×240, model in lcd.rs)
12	//!   0x1180_0-    USB
13	//!   0x1210_0-    UART1 (MIDI IN)
14	//!   0x1310_0-    ADC
15	//!   0x1eee000-   interrupt controller (0x1eee008 bit14 = ready, polled by the
16	//!                RAM early-init; the rest stored bits)
17	//!   0x1eee240    DBG_MSG debug box (console)
18	//!   0x01f0_0000  SRAM banks (256 KiB; cleared by the early init, config block at 0x1f28000)
19	//!   0x01c0xxxx 'negative' long-call targets are RAM-resident .data code
20	//!   (copied from flash 0x02084820 by the CRT), not a mask ROM
21	//!
22	//! Policy: unknown MMIO accesses are logged and return a benign default —
23	//! never silently swallowed. The access log is the reverse-engineering
24	//! roadmap.
